  "description": "PEYVAU crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C144 H166 Eu2 N4 O26 Ti4. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Ti1 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti8 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti2 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti7 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Ti4 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti6 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti5 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti3 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.848-3.811 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.20-142.56°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Eu2Ti4(μ2-O)2(μ3-O)4(−pbpy)2(4-tbba)10. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ2-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
